  "changesets": [
    {
      "releases": [
        {
          "name": "@tangleai/agents",
          "type": "patch"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "The agent replays every tool call with object arguments, the ones it ran with: a call a model sent with empty, non-object or malformed arguments goes back as `{}`, in this turn and from a stored history. A provider that keeps tool input as an object (Anthropic's, through a router such as OpenRouter) refused the next turn of such a conversation with HTTP 400.",
      "id": "replay-object-arguments"
    },
    {
      "releases": [
        {
          "name": "@tangleai/os",
          "type": "patch"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "A document module's form works in its sandboxed frame. The frame has no form submission (an authored document cannot send a form anywhere), and the browser refused a submission before the form's submit event, so a document's `on.submit` never ran: To do could not add an item. The module host now turns a submit button and Enter in a field into the form's submit event, after the form's own validity check; nothing navigates. The authoring gate refuses `$apply` over computed items when every rule matches by path (they match no rule and show nothing), and the crib says how to show one item by its position.",
      "id": "sandboxed-forms"
    }
  ],
